    "result_text": "Tests green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agree with the finding. The raw `\"-\"` literal in `AssignCustomerCode` reintroduced exactly the separator drift `CustomerCode` was designed to prevent \u2014 its `SEPARATOR` is private and `format`/`region` are a deliberately matched pair.\n\n- **`CustomerCode.java`**: added `withSuffix(String base, int n)`, which joins with the private `SEPARATOR`, keeping every customerCode spelling rule in the one class that owns them (now unit-testable alongside `format`/`hash8`/`region`/`checkDigit`).\n- **`AssignCustomerCode.java`**: the loop now calls `CustomerCode.withSuffix(base, n)` instead of `base + \"-\" + n`. The repository scan and the \"pick smallest free `n` \u2265 2\" loop stay here at the orchestration altitude, as suggested.\n\nFull suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and acceptance behaviour is unchanged.",
