        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe orchestration placement is fine \u2014 ensuring uniqueness at the moment the code is assigned needs the `OwnerRepository`, and this step already owns \"produce the owner's customerCode,\" so de-duplication living here is natural. The problem is where the *string shaping* of the de-duplicated code lives.\n\nFinding \u2014 suffix formatting duplicates `CustomerCode`'s separator and bypasses its \"single source of truth\" role:\n\n- `CustomerCode` is documented as the \"Single source of truth for an owner's `customerCode` and the values derived from it,\" and goes out of its way to keep the dash in one place: `SEPARATOR = '-'` is private, `format(...)`/`region(...)` are described as a \"matched pair\" that \"cannot drift apart.\" The new code reintroduces a raw `\"-\"` literal in `AssignCustomerCode:43` (`base + \"-\" + n`). That is precisely the drift the model was built to prevent: change `SEPARATOR` to anything else and you get `NSW_1A2B3C4D-2` \u2014 a region/hash joined with the new separator but the dedup suffix still a dash. The suffix-joining dash is semantically the same separator and should come from the same source.\n\n- The de-dup *formatting* (how a disambiguated code is spelled: `base + SEPARATOR + n`, starting at 2) is customerCode-shaping logic and belongs on `CustomerCode` alongside `format`/`hash8`/`region`/`checkDigit`, not open-coded in a pipeline step. Suggest a small helper there, e.g. `CustomerCode.deduplicate(String base, Set<String> existing)` (or `withSuffix(base, n)`), so `AssignCustomerCode` reduces to: build the base, gather existing codes, call the helper. That keeps `AssignCustomerCode` at the orchestration altitude (load repo state, delegate the string rule) and keeps every customerCode spelling rule in the one class that owns them. It also makes the suffix rule unit-testable next to the other code rules.\n\nNet: move the `\"-\" + n` suffix construction into `CustomerCode` (reusing `SEPARATOR`); leave the repository scan and the \"pick smallest free n\" loop in `AssignCustomerCode` driving that helper."
